   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( h(x) = x^{2} + 1 \\). The functions f and g satisfy \\( \\lim_{x \\to 1} f(x) = 2 \\) and \\( \\lim_{x \\to 1} g(x) = -4 \\), and selected values of f and g are given in the table. Find \\( \\lim_{x \\to 1} \\frac{h(f(x))}{g(x)} \\). Name the limit theorems you use.",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
